Defaults are used only when the destructured value is `undefined`.

**Spread** (`...arr`) expands an iterable into individual elements — used in calls or literals.
**Rest** (`...args`) collects multiple arguments into an array — used in function parameter lists.
```js
// Spread
Math.max(...[1, 2, 3]);
// Rest
function sum(...nums) { return nums.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0); }
```

